KZ3 patch 1048 (SPU pass 34, RE pass 70 section 5, 71): KZ3_SPURS_RUN_MS policy-module run budget (default 0 = off): past it the selectWorkload intercept answers 'another workload' so the module exits by its own path; past twice it a lane still at a GETLLAR or channel-read tick site is halted; the kernel joins the lanes, releases the claim and re-dispatches the lane at 0xA00 later; spu_pm_ctx_describe_resv for the stuck report.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): context only (upstream v0.18.0 changed lines around the hunks; same change).

